/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (A person who manages to recognize, accept and channel their own emotions usually also has a freer and more agile body. Because the freedom of the body does not begin in the muscles, it manifests there; freedom begins in the emotions.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (If we work only to release physical tension, while continuing to produce the same inner conflicts, we create a vicious circle that feeds itself. The source remains untouched and the body continues to speak the language of emotions that the mind has not yet managed to hear.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
173 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (Emotions are the alchemical laboratory where human experience is transformed into consciousness; there the breath takes form in the soul and the soul finds expression in the body. When they are accepted, understood and transformed, a person becomes lighter, freer and more authentic.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (It is precisely here that the origin of art also lies. Art was not born as an ornament of life, but as a need to process what a person could no longer keep only inside themselves. Song, poetry, painting, dance and theater are languages of the soul, ways to transform emotion into creation. In this process, what could have been a burden for the body became beauty, meaning and freedom.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (This is the deepest function of art: to transform emotion into consciousness, the soul into expression and the body from a carrier of the weight of unexpressed emotions into a free instrument of creation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
